{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-sqrt-q-ribbon-structure","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:sqrt-q-ribbon-structure","kind":"remark","title":"The element $\\sqrt{q}$ and the ribbon structure","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-braiding-eigenvalue-extraction","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-tqft-context"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-braiding-eigenvalue-extraction","tags":["ribbon","twist","sqrt-q","tqft","framed-links","braiding","eigenvalue"],"text":"sqrt-q-ribbon-structure.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:sqrt-q-ribbon-structure\"></a><p>The element <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v := q^{1/2}</code> constitutes post-Archimedean naming. A ribbon structure on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code> demands a natural twist <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varTheta_V \\colon V \\xrightarrow{\\sim} V</code>. On the defining <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{SU}_q(2)</code> representation, the twist axiom forces <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varTheta_V = q^{1/2}\\mathrm{id}_V</code>. The binary sign choice on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v</code> dictates the spin structure on the realized worldline.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/sqrt-q-ribbon-structure.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.25.2","page":"b/rem-sqrt-q-ribbon-structure","qa":{"counts":{"pass":57,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
